# Files excluded from the customer zip.
#
# Every pattern here is matched by rsync --exclude, which matches at ANY depth
# unless the pattern is anchored with a leading slash. That is deliberate for
# things like .git and node_modules, and dangerous for short generic names -
# a bare `src` would strip a bundled library's own src/ directory as well as
# the plugin's. Anchor anything generic.
#
# What must NOT be listed here, however tempting: edd-license/ and
# lib/wbcom-settings/. Both are committed RUNTIME code, not development
# dependencies - composer does not restore them on a customer's site, so if
# they are not in the zip they are not on their site, and licensing and the
# settings screen break on every fresh install.

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.vscode
.idea
*.code-workspace

# CI and code-quality config
.github
.phpcs.xml
.phpcs.xml.dist
phpcs.xml
phpcs.xml.dist
phpunit.xml
phpunit.xml.dist
phpstan.neon
phpstan.neon.dist
.travis.yml

# Node and build tooling. The minified and RTL assets are COMMITTED, so the
# zip needs no build step - only the tooling that would regenerate them is
# excluded.
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
gruntfile.js
Gruntfile.js
webpack.config.js

# Every markdown file, at any depth.
#
# A wildcard rather than a list of filenames. Naming them one at a time means
# anything added later ships by default, and that is not hypothetical: the
# sibling Price Quote plugin shipped an internal QA report carrying a local dev
# URL, and its Pro half shipped a competitive audit, to every customer.
# Customer documentation is README.txt; working notes belong in docs/.
*.md

# Working notes and internal docs
/plan
/docs
/audit

# Build inputs and outputs
/bin
/dist
/tests
.distignore
.contract-audit-baseline.json

# Tooling scratch that is gitignored but still on disk.
#
# .distignore is applied by rsync against the WORKING TREE, not against git's
# index, so "it is in .gitignore" is not protection - a gitignored directory
# sitting on disk ships anyway. .autovap-wt holds full worktree copies of the
# plugin, 2.8M of duplicate code, and would have gone out in the zip.
.autovap-wt
.worktrees
*.log

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
